<!--
    Widget strings only. Everything the Flutter side owns stays in its
    ARB files; these are drawn by native code in a process the Flutter
    engine may never have started in, so `l10n` is not reachable.

    Indonesian is `values-in`, not `values-id`: resource qualifiers use
    the legacy ISO code, which is what `Locale.getLanguage()` returns
    on every Android version.
-->
